# Secrets and credentials
#
# Broad by design: an environment file that reaches a public repository cannot
# be un-published, so the default is to exclude every shape of one and to name
# the exceptions explicitly below.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*token.json*
*credentials.json*
credentials.json
.credentials
*.key
*.pem
memory/test_credentials.md

# frontend/.env is NOT a secret and MUST stay in version control.
#
# It carries three build-time flags, none of them credentials. One of them is
# load-bearing: without INLINE_RUNTIME_CHUNK=false, Create React App inlines the
# webpack runtime as an inline <script>, our own `script-src 'self'` blocks it,
# and the site serves a blank page to every visitor. That failure has already
# happened once on this project, for exactly this reason — `*.env` above swept
# the file out of a clean clone, and the clone could not deploy.
#
# The negation must stay AFTER the patterns above; git honours the last rule
# that matches. frontend/.env.local and every other frontend/.env.* remain
# ignored, which is where a local override with anything sensitive belongs.
!frontend/.env

# Local Cowork safety snapshots (not for repo)
_backups/
